---
description: AI provider isolation, prompts, and untrusted model output
globs: backend/app/ai/**/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

Business modules call an AI application interface. They do not import
OpenAI, Gemini, Anthropic, or other provider SDKs.

Keep provider configuration, request formats, response parsing, and provider
errors inside `app/ai/`. Map provider payloads into application types before
they leave that boundary.

Keep prompts and orchestration in the AI layer. Do not put prompts in
FastAPI routers.

Treat model output as untrusted input. Validate structured responses with
typed schemas before a business workflow uses them. Do not let raw model
text trigger a sensitive operation without validation and authorization.

Handle timeouts, connection errors, invalid responses, and provider errors
explicitly. Do not add retries unless the task requires them.

Do not log prompts or responses that contain secrets, tokens, or sensitive
personal data.
